@startuml
title Why both surfaces are empty: the label tracks a feed you cannot trigger

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #555
  FontSize 12
}

legend top left
  <b>Recap</b> = Claude Code's away_summary, end-of-turn prose. We read it. We cannot ask for one.
  <b>Floor</b> = a label derived locally at hook time, so a pane is never blank. Does not exist today.
  Verified: __claude_pane_label.sh :204 :239 :243 :251 :264 :274 :317 :319
            Notes/areas/tmux-pane-label-design.md "Out of Scope" + cadence table
            ~/.codex/hooks.json event list
endlegend

rectangle "CLAUDE PANE   (live: this pane, %63)" as C {
  rectangle "UserPromptSubmit\n:204 state ONLY, never a label" as UPS #C8E6C9
  rectangle "Stop\n:239 the only label writer" as STOP #C8E6C9

  rectangle "ALWAYS written, every single turn\n:251 @claude_state = working / idle\n:264 @claude_glyph = : ▶ ▪ ◌\n\nLIVE NOW: state=working  glyph=▶  <b>this half works</b>" as ALWAYS #C8E6C9

  rectangle "is there a recap in the transcript?\n:243 latest_summary(transcript)\n\nLIVE NOW: <b>0 records</b>" as SRC #FFCDD2

  rectangle ":274   if [[ -n $label ]]" as GATE #FFE0B2

  rectangle "NEVER written this session\n:317 @claude_goal   -> tmux status line\n:319 @claude_label  -> pane border\n\nLIVE NOW: <b>both empty</b>  <b>this half is dark</b>" as NEVER #FFCDD2
}

UPS --> ALWAYS
STOP --> ALWAYS
STOP --> SRC
SRC --> GATE
GATE --> NEVER

note right of SRC
  Needs roughly 3 minutes of your silence.
  Your own doc measured it: 35 recaps,
  min 184s, median 200s, max 362s,
  0 of 35 under 60s.

  And states the consequence outright:
  "A session where the user keeps typing
   produces none at all."

  You have typed continuously all session.
  So: none. The system is correct.
end note

rectangle "CODEX PANE" as X #FFCDD2 {
  rectangle "events it HAS:\n  PreToolUse  PostToolUse  UserPromptSubmit\n  SessionStart  SessionEnd  SubagentStart/Stop\n\nevent it does NOT have:\n  <b>Stop / turn-end</b>" as XEV
  rectangle "__claude_pane_label.sh is wired into NONE of them.\nstate, glyph, goal, label: all absent, always." as XN
}
XEV --> XN

note bottom of X
  Your doc, Out of Scope:
  "Codex panes have hooks but no away_summary,
   so they stay unlabelled."

  Your stated expectation ("claude or codex MUST
  always have those") contradicts this line.
end note

rectangle "WHERE A SECOND SOURCE WOULD GO\nfeeds the gate when no recap exists, never overwrites one\n\nAlready tried and reverted:\n  newest prompt wins  -> echoed your keyboard forever  (9141d48)\n  frozen first prompt -> froze on 'list my open prs'\n  last assistant msg  -> 'Now let me create memories...'  (45f17a4)\n\nNot yet tried:\n  <b>ornith on the Mac summarises the transcript tail on Stop</b>\n  costs no conversation turn, no frontier quota, always available" as FLOOR #E1BEE7

GATE ..> FLOOR : the branch that does not exist today

@enduml
